KeybindStuff.DashHelp: Double tap a movement key

NPCs: {
	Edgelord: {
		DisplayName: Curse Thief
		DisplayName1: Edgelord
		DeathCurse: Morden's Curse has left...
		Census.SpawnCondition: Always available, spawned on world creation
		DyingText: HELP!
		Deviantt: I can't help much with this arcane stuff, talk to that Morden guy.

		Chat: {
			Intro: Hello, {0}.
			Grave: That grave. It once belonged to a good friend of ours, Tucker.
			AskHelp: I have a great power, and a great curse. If you ever need my help, do not be afraid to ask at any time.
			OldManTalk: I heard of a cursed old man residing in the dungeon and went to see him. His curse seems to be of a different nature than mine, but he is as immortal as I.
			Hello: Hello again.
			Water: It seems like all the water in this world is full of magic. With my curse, it's best I avoid it, but with such a large amount of magic in the enviroment, this truly has become an Arcane Adventure... no, an Odyssey.
			StrongWarrior: That weapon you're holding... you must have become quite the Strong Warrior. Talk to me if you need help using it.
		}

		Help: {
			Relics: Relics are quite interesting. They function as an imbue, as well as a weapon that can channel magic.
			Early1: Those with a strong sense of justice or an affinity for magic are granted Poseidon's Spirit. Slaying extremely powerful magic users may cause some of their power to be released, creating one of these.
			EarlyMagic1: Magic can be used to enchant compatible items, but to properly use it you will have to craft spell scrolls. Try crafting magic-conductive paper at a sawmill with gel and wood.
			EarlyMagic2: Some spells can be charged up to increase their power. Do think before you do, as you leave yourself vulnerable while charging.
			EarlyMagic3: You can imbue your items with your magic or fighting style quite easily. If you do, you'll have different weapon stats, and you may even be able to apply debuffs to your enemies.
			EarlyFighting1: You can enhance your body with trace magic to use fighting styles, but technique scrolls are needed to use your full power. Try crafting paper at a sawmill with gel and wood.
			EarlyFighting2: Some techniques allow you to launch yourself in a direction, depending on the type you can [{0} or {1}].
			WorldofMagic: This World is full of Magic. However, those who can freely channel mana into non-magical items like us are paragons.
			StackImbues: With multiple imbues, you can stack them on eachother to allow scrolls or special items to use both imbues at the same time. For example, a Relic can be imbued into a Magic, or a Magic can be imbued into a Fighting Style.
			PreHard1: It's said there's some abomination deep, deep underground that contains a large amount of magic power. It might be benificial to obtain this power.
			PreHard2: You should learn what goes well with your magic. Some weapons or abilities might work better or worse with it.
			EarlyHard1: Killing that beast should have granted you some of it's power in the form of a sigil. You should use that if you haven't already.
			EarlyHard2: Fishing in the ocean can grant you all sorts of goods, but a major find is metal that has absorbed magic that has seeped into the water.
			DarkSeaWarning: Beware of travelling beyond the bounds of this world, going far enough out to sea might well spell your doom.
			BronzeTip: Bronze can be created using {0} and {1} and some sort of chaotic material.=
			CultistTip: I can feel the presence of a powerful magic user, one whose mastery far surpasses ours. Please, check out the dungeon.
			NothingToSay: I don't have anything to say right now.
			SunkenWeapon: Although made of Arcanium metal, that sword in your hand doesn't seem to conduct your magic any better than a regular weapon. Instead, it looks like it contains its own magic granted to it by centuries under the sea.
			EvanderWarning: It seems a bounty has been placed on your head due to your actions. Do be careful venturing out too far...
			HasStrengthWeapon: I see you've got your hands on a strength weapons. These weapons are too heavy for regular warriors, and so users must learn to use a fighting style. Coincidentally, these weapons bring out the power of your fighting style in ways not seen in anything else.
			CannonFist: Having your own cannonballs can make Cannon Fist far more effective.
			SailorStyle: Sailor Style relies on the magic in water to empower yourself. Try stepping in the water or drinking a healing drink while using it.
			WeaponSkills: Some weapons have special skills, make good use of them.
			ArtisinalWeapon: Some weapons are made with such mastery that imbuing them with magic would be detrimental. These are known as Artisinal Weapons.
		}

		TownNPCMood: {
			Content: I have no issues at the moment.
			NoHome: Although I'm usually travelling, it would be nice to have a place to rest.
			FarFromHome: I'm quite far from camp, aren't I?
			LoveSpace: It's quite peaceful here.
			DislikeCrowded: There are quite a lot of people here.
			HateCrowded: This place is absolutely crammed.
			LoveBiome: I love {BiomeName}, it's so open and free.
			LikeBiome: Hm, {BiomeName} reminds me of Sameria, not a bad thing at all.
			DislikeBiome: I must complain, {BiomeName} is so cold.
			HateBiome: You would really put me in {BiomeName}, after everything we've been through?!
			LikeNPC: "{NPCName} is a kind old man, like Enzior."
			LoveNPC: "{NPCName} and I have quite a few things in common, we get along very well."
			DislikeNPC: "{NPCName} is a pirate, something that I've had some negative experiences with out at sea."
			HateNPC: "{NPCName} disgusts me with such experiments."
			LikeNPC_Princess: "{NPCName} really shows me that not all royalty are wicked, quite respectable."
			Princess_LovesNPC: "{NPCName} used to look at me funny, but we get along quite well now!"
		}
	}

	Evander: {
		DisplayName: Evander, the Mountainbreaker
		DeathMessage: Evander, the Mountainbreaker has been defeated!
		SpawnInfo: Spawns naturally in Hardmode, in the outer forests of the world. Spawning decreased reduced after being defeated.
	}

	DebuffDummy.DisplayName: Debuff Dummy
}

