CodebreakerDialogOption: {
	Name: The Dark Sea
	Description1: This planet is abundant with magic, to a scale of which has never been recorded even among auric dragons and true gods.
	Description2: A majority of the world has been devastated by this magic. This may have not always been the case however, as the erotion patterns suggest the large amount of mana manifested a mere eight hundred years ago.
	Description3: Long before my creation, the only ones left that still know the answers would be: The cursed ones of old, who are scattered across the world - Xeroc, who has been unaccounted for - Yharon, who still needs much more time to revive.
	Description4: As a Paragon, I regret to convey that you possess more knowledge about magic than I.
	DemiDescription1: While observing you, I have learned many things about the past of this planet. The amount of energy needed to create the "fracture" far exceeds what any current living being can output, barring the traitor almighty.
	DemiDescription2: A majority of the world has been devastated by this "fracture". This was long before my creation. Of course, I had no issue finding the source of the great mana storm.
	DemiDescription3: Attempts to approach the Dark Sea Epicentre have been unsuccessful, as I lose control of my machines due to the interferance and magical corruption.
	DemiDescription4: As a demigod, I regret to convey that you possess more knowledge about methods to approach such a place than I.
}

